IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mig-prot-dates`
IMPORT `mig-protection`

-- Migration Act 1958 (Cth), the asylum seeker's questions -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. Every expected value was written by hand from the deposited text before the run. The people
-- and facts are HYPOTHETICAL. Calendar: 2 November 2026 is a Monday; 25 December 2026 and 1 January 2027 are Fridays.

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar day` d m y

GIVEN r IS A DEONTIC `Protection party` `Protection step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ends fulfilled` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixtures
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, ci IS A BOOLEAN, cii IS A BOOLEAN, ciii IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My social group`
`group of` a b ci cii ciii d MEANS `My social group` WITH
    `every member of the group shares a characteristic` IS a
    `I share the characteristic, or am perceived as sharing it` IS b
    `the characteristic is innate or immutable` IS ci
    `the characteristic is so fundamental to identity or conscience that no member should be forced to renounce it` IS cii
    `the characteristic distinguishes the group from society` IS ciii
    `the characteristic is a fear of persecution` IS d

`a group of gay men` MEANS `group of` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a group set apart by society only` MEANS `group of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a loose set of people with nothing in common` MEANS `group of` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a group defined by its fear` MEANS `group of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A BOOLEAN, acc IS A BOOLEAN, dur IS A BOOLEAN, st IS A BOOLEAN, inst IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Protection in my country`
`protection of` a w acc dur st inst MEANS `Protection in my country` WITH
    `protection could be provided by the State, or by a party or organisation controlling the State or a substantial part of its territory` IS a
    `the protector is willing to offer it` IS w
    `I can access the protection` IS acc
    `the protection is durable` IS dur
    `the protector is the State` IS st
    `the State has an appropriate criminal law, a reasonably effective police force and an impartial judicial system` IS inst

`no protection at home` MEANS `protection of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`an unwilling State` MEANS `protection of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a State with working courts and police` MEANS `protection of` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a willing State without working institutions` MEANS `protection of` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a controlling militia that protects durably` MEANS `protection of` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a controlling militia with fleeting protection` MEANS `protection of` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN rsn IS A `Reason for the persecution I fear`, grp IS A `My social group`, chance IS A BOOLEAN, areas IS A BOOLEAN, ess IS A BOOLEAN, hm IS A `Harm I fear`, sys IS A BOOLEAN, prot IS A `Protection in my country`, chg IS A `Change in my behaviour`, cond IS A BOOLEAN, sat IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My fear of persecution`
`fear of` rsn grp chance areas ess hm sys prot chg cond sat MEANS `My fear of persecution` WITH
    `the reason` IS rsn
    `the social group` IS grp
    `there is a real chance I would be persecuted for that reason if I returned` IS chance
    `the real chance relates to all areas of the country` IS areas
    `that reason is the essential and significant reason for the persecution` IS ess
    `the harm feared` IS hm
    `the persecution involves systematic and discriminatory conduct` IS sys
    `the protection available` IS prot
    `the change that would avoid it` IS chg
    `the real chance depends on conduct I engaged in in Australia` IS cond
    `I satisfy the Minister I engaged in that conduct otherwise than to strengthen my claim` IS sat

`no change` MEANS `no reasonable change in my behaviour would avoid a real chance of persecution`

-- Amina (HYPOTHETICAL), a journalist who fears imprisonment and death for her reporting, from a country whose
-- government does the persecuting.
`Amina's fear` MEANS `fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE

GIVEN f IS A `My fear of persecution`, here IS A BOOLEAN, outside IS A BOOLEAN, unable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My refugee claim`
`claim of` f here outside unable MEANS `My refugee claim` WITH
    `I am in Australia` IS here
    `I am outside my country of nationality (or, if I have none, of former habitual residence)` IS outside
    `owing to my fear I am unable or unwilling to seek that country's protection (or, if stateless, to return to it)` IS unable
    `my fear` IS f

`Amina's claim` MEANS `claim of` `Amina's fear` TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN wc IS A BOOLEAN, npc IS A BOOLEAN, un IS A BOOLEAN, asio IS A BOOLEAN, dsec IS A BOOLEAN, conv IS A `My conviction`, dcom IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Security and crime facts`
`security of` wc npc un asio dsec conv dcom MEANS `Security and crime facts` WITH
    `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I committed a crime against peace, a war crime or a crime against humanity` IS wc
    `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I committed a serious non-political crime before entering Australia` IS npc
    `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I have been guilty of acts contrary to the purposes and principles of the United Nations` IS un
    `ASIO has assessed me to be directly or indirectly a risk to security` IS asio
    `the Minister considers on reasonable grounds I am a danger to Australia's security` IS dsec
    `my conviction by final judgment` IS conv
    `the Minister considers on reasonable grounds I am a danger to the Australian community` IS dcom

`no conviction` MEANS `no conviction by final judgment of a particularly serious crime`
`nothing found` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no conviction` FALSE
`war crimes reasons` MEANS `security of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no conviction` FALSE
`a serious non-political crime` MEANS `security of` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no conviction` FALSE
`acts against the United Nations` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no conviction` FALSE
`an ASIO adverse assessment` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no conviction` FALSE
`a danger to security` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no conviction` FALSE
`convicted of a serious Australian offence and a danger` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a serious Australian offence` TRUE
`convicted of a serious foreign offence, not a danger` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a serious foreign offence` FALSE
`thought a danger without a conviction` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no conviction` TRUE
`convicted of another particularly serious crime and a danger` MEANS `security of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another particularly serious crime` TRUE

GIVEN here IS A BOOLEAN, grounds IS A BOOLEAN, hm IS A `Harm I face if removed`, reloc IS A BOOLEAN, auth IS A BOOLEAN, gen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My complementary protection claim`
`complementary of` here grounds hm reloc auth gen MEANS `My complementary protection claim` WITH
    `I am in Australia` IS here
    `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing that, as a necessary and foreseeable consequence of my removal, there is a real risk I will suffer the harm` IS grounds
    `the harm I face` IS hm
    `the Minister is satisfied it would be reasonable for me to relocate to an area of the country without that risk` IS reloc
    `the Minister is satisfied I could obtain protection from an authority of the country that removes the risk` IS auth
    `the Minister is satisfied the risk is faced by the population generally and not by me personally` IS gen

-- Bilal (HYPOTHETICAL), sentenced to death at home for a non-political offence, facing execution if removed.
`Bilal's claim` MEANS `complementary of` TRUE TRUE `the death penalty carried out on me` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a claim the Minister rejects` MEANS `complementary of` TRUE FALSE `torture` FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN r IS A BOOLEAN, steps IS A BOOLEAN, fp IS A BOOLEAN, rr IS A BOOLEAN, fret IS A BOOLEAN, pers IS A BOOLEAN, rro IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My right to live in another country`
`right of` r steps fp rr fret pers rro MEANS `My right to live in another country` WITH
    `I have a right to enter and reside in a country other than Australia` IS r
    `I have taken all possible steps to avail myself of that right` IS steps
    `I have a well-founded fear of persecution in that country for a Convention reason` IS fp
    `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing I would face a real risk of significant harm in that country` IS rr
    `I have a well-founded fear that country would return me to another country` IS fret
    `I would be persecuted in that other country for a Convention reason` IS pers
    `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing I would face a real risk of significant harm in that other country` IS rro

`no right elsewhere` MEANS `right of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an unused right to live in a safe country` MEANS `right of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN mem IS A BOOLEAN, how IS A `How my family member holds their protection visa`, same IS A BOOLEAN, before IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My family member's protection visa`
`family of` mem how same before MEANS `My family member's protection visa` WITH
    `I am a member of the same family unit as a person who holds a protection visa` IS mem
    `how they hold it` IS how
    `their visa is of the same class as the one I applied for` IS same
    `I applied before they were granted their visa` IS before

`no family visa` MEANS `family of` FALSE `I have no family member holding a protection visa` FALSE FALSE
`a refugee husband, applied together` MEANS `family of` TRUE `as a refugee (s 36(2)(a))` TRUE TRUE
`a complementary protection mother, applied together` MEANS `family of` TRUE `on complementary protection (s 36(2)(aa))` TRUE TRUE
`a refugee husband, applied after his grant` MEANS `family of` TRUE `as a refugee (s 36(2)(a))` TRUE FALSE
`a refugee husband with a visa of another class` MEANS `family of` TRUE `as a refugee (s 36(2)(a))` FALSE TRUE

-- A claim that fails as a refugee claim (no Convention reason): Bilal's.
`Bilal's refugee claim` MEANS `claim of` (`fear of` `none of these reasons` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A refugee claim the Act leaves open (harm outside the s 5J(5) instances).
`an open refugee claim` MEANS `claim of` (`fear of` `religion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `harm of another kind` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5AAA
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Is it up to me to make out my claim question` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is it up to me to make out my claim question` FALSE))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5J(5): serious harm (the list does not limit; other harm NOTHING)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `a threat to my life or liberty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `significant physical harassment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `significant physical ill-treatment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `significant economic hardship that threatens my capacity to subsist` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `denial of access to basic services that threatens my capacity to subsist` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `denial of capacity to earn a livelihood of any kind that threatens my capacity to subsist` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `harm of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5L: particular social group
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Am I a member of a particular social group question` `a group of gay men`
#ASSERT `Am I a member of a particular social group question` `a group set apart by society only`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I a member of a particular social group question` `a loose set of people with nothing in common`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I a member of a particular social group question` `a group defined by its fear`))
-- (c) fails: shared, perceived, but none of (i)-(iii).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I a member of a particular social group question` (`group of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
-- (b) fails: I neither share nor am perceived to share the characteristic.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I a member of a particular social group question` (`group of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5LA: effective protection measures
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` `no protection at home` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` `an unwilling State` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` `a State with working courts and police` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` `a willing State without working institutions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` `a controlling militia that protects durably` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` `a controlling militia with fleeting protection` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Protection I cannot access: (2)(a) fails, ability left open.
#ASSERT `Are effective protection measures available to me question` (`protection of` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5J(3): changing behaviour
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `no change`))
#ASSERT `Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `a reasonable change of another kind would avoid it`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `a change conflicting with a characteristic fundamental to my identity or conscience`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `a change concealing an innate or immutable characteristic of mine`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `altering or concealing my religious beliefs, renouncing a conversion, or ceasing to practise my faith`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `concealing my race, ethnicity, nationality or country of origin`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `altering or concealing my political beliefs`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `concealing a physical, psychological or intellectual disability`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `entering or remaining in a marriage I oppose, or accepting the forced marriage of a child`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `altering or concealing my sexual orientation, gender identity or intersex status`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5J: well-founded fear
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` `Amina's fear` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(a): no Convention reason.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `none of these reasons` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Family as the social group: s 5K, not encoded.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `membership of my family as a particular social group` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A social group that meets s 5L, and one that does not.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `membership of a particular social group other than my family` `a group of gay men` TRUE TRUE TRUE `significant physical ill-treatment` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `membership of a particular social group other than my family` `a group defined by its fear` TRUE TRUE TRUE `significant physical ill-treatment` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b), (1)(c): no real chance; not all areas.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` FALSE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE FALSE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(a), (4)(c): not the essential and significant reason; not systematic and discriminatory.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` FALSE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(b), (5): harm of another kind is left open...
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `harm of another kind` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ...unless another element is a definite no.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `none of these reasons` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `harm of another kind` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): effective protection available; left open.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `a State with working courts and police` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `a willing State without working institutions` `no change` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): a protected change does not defeat the fear; another reasonable change does.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `membership of a particular social group other than my family` `a group of gay men` TRUE TRUE TRUE `significant physical ill-treatment` TRUE `no protection at home` `altering or concealing my sexual orientation, gender identity or intersex status` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `a reasonable change of another kind would avoid it` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): conduct in Australia disregarded unless I satisfy the Minister.
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` (`fear of` `political opinion` `a loose set of people with nothing in common` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a threat to my life or liberty` TRUE `no protection at home` `no change` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5H: refugee
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `Amina's claim` `nothing found` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` (`claim of` `Amina's fear` FALSE TRUE TRUE) `nothing found` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` (`claim of` `Amina's fear` TRUE FALSE TRUE) `nothing found` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` (`claim of` `Amina's fear` TRUE TRUE FALSE) `nothing found` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `Amina's claim` `war crimes reasons` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `Amina's claim` `a serious non-political crime` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `Amina's claim` `acts against the United Nations` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 5H(2) speaks only of the Minister's serious reasons; an ASIO assessment or danger does not stop me being a refugee.
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `Amina's claim` `an ASIO adverse assessment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `an open refugee claim` `nothing found` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `an open refugee claim` `war crimes reasons` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a refugee question` `Bilal's refugee claim` `nothing found` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 36(2A), (2)(aa): complementary protection
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Is the harm I face significant harm question` `arbitrary deprivation of my life`
#ASSERT `Is the harm I face significant harm question` `the death penalty carried out on me`
#ASSERT `Is the harm I face significant harm question` `torture`
#ASSERT `Is the harm I face significant harm question` `cruel or inhuman treatment or punishment`
#ASSERT `Is the harm I face significant harm question` `degrading treatment or punishment`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is the harm I face significant harm question` `harm of some other kind`))

#ASSERT `Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `nothing found` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `nothing found` TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` (`complementary of` FALSE TRUE `the death penalty carried out on me` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `nothing found` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `a claim the Minister rejects` `nothing found` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` (`complementary of` TRUE TRUE `harm of some other kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `nothing found` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` (`complementary of` TRUE TRUE `torture` TRUE FALSE FALSE) `nothing found` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` (`complementary of` TRUE TRUE `torture` FALSE TRUE FALSE) `nothing found` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` (`complementary of` TRUE TRUE `torture` FALSE FALSE TRUE) `nothing found` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `war crimes reasons` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `a danger to security` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `convicted of a serious Australian offence and a danger` FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `convicted of another particularly serious crime and a danger` FALSE))
-- A conviction without the Minister's view of danger, or a view of danger without a conviction, is not (2C)(b)(ii).
#ASSERT `Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `convicted of a serious foreign offence, not a danger` FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `Bilal's claim` `thought a danger without a conviction` FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 36(3)-(5A): a right to live in another country
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` `no right elsewhere`))
#ASSERT `Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` `an unused right to live in a safe country`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)))
-- A fear of being sent on, but nothing to fear in the other country: (3) still applies.
#ASSERT `Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Persecution in the other country, but no fear of being sent there: (3) still applies.
#ASSERT `Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` (`right of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 36, s 91WB: the Act's criteria
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Amina's claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `yes: as a refugee to whom Australia owes protection (s 36(1A), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Amina's claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `an ASIO adverse assessment` EQUALS `no: ASIO has assessed me as a risk to security (s 36(1B))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Amina's claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `a danger to security` EQUALS `no: the Minister considers me a danger to security or, after a particularly serious crime, to the community (s 36(1C))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Amina's claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `convicted of a serious Australian offence and a danger` EQUALS `no: the Minister considers me a danger to security or, after a particularly serious crime, to the community (s 36(1C))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Amina's claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `an unused right to live in a safe country` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `Bilal's claim` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `yes: on complementary protection (s 36(1A), (2)(aa))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `Bilal's claim` `an unused right to live in a safe country` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `an open refugee claim` `Bilal's claim` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `yes: as a refugee or on complementary protection, whichever the Minister finds (s 36(1A), (2)(a) or (aa))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `an open refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `not covered: whether I am a refugee turns on a point the Act leaves open`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `a refugee husband, applied together` `nothing found` EQUALS `yes: as a member of the family unit of a refugee who holds a protection visa (s 36(1A), (2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `a complementary protection mother, applied together` `nothing found` EQUALS `yes: as a member of the family unit of a complementary protection visa holder (s 36(1A), (2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `a refugee husband, applied after his grant` `nothing found` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `a refugee husband with a visa of another class` `nothing found` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` FALSE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `a refugee husband, applied together` `nothing found` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `nothing found` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
-- War-crimes reasons exclude both the refugee route (5H(2)) and complementary protection (36(2C)(a)).
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Amina's claim` `Bilal's claim` `no right elsewhere` `no family visa` `war crimes reasons` EQUALS `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
-- The family route still needs (1B) and (1C).
#ASSERT `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` TRUE `Bilal's refugee claim` `a claim the Minister rejects` `no right elsewhere` `a refugee husband, applied together` `an ASIO adverse assessment` EQUALS `no: ASIO has assessed me as a risk to security (s 36(1B))`

-- s 36A
#ASSERT `Must the Minister first record whether I am owed protection question` TRUE `no family visa`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must the Minister first record whether I am owed protection question` FALSE `no family visa`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must the Minister first record whether I am owed protection question` TRUE `a refugee husband, applied together`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must the Minister first record whether I am owed protection question` TRUE `a complementary protection mother, applied together`))
#ASSERT `Must the Minister first record whether I am owed protection question` TRUE `a refugee husband, applied after his grant`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5AA: unauthorised maritime arrival
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIVEN sea IS A BOOLEAN, unl IS A BOOLEAN, nz IS A BOOLEAN, nf IS A BOOLEAN, pr IS A BOOLEAN, born IS A BOOLEAN, par IS A BOOLEAN, cit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How I came to Australia`
`arrival of` sea unl nz nf pr born par cit MEANS `How I came to Australia` WITH
    `I entered Australia by sea at a place and time s 5AA(1)(a) covers` IS sea
    `I became an unlawful non-citizen because of that entry` IS unl
    `I am a New Zealand citizen who held and produced a New Zealand passport in force` IS nz
    `I held and produced a passport in force and am ordinarily resident on Norfolk Island` IS nf
    `I am in a class of persons the regulations prescribe as excluded maritime arrivals` IS pr
    `I was born in the migration zone` IS born
    `a parent of mine was an unauthorised maritime arrival under s 5AA(1) when I was born` IS par
    `I was an Australian citizen at birth` IS cit

